  "quirks": {
    "game_btn": "at font scale 1 the label prints with the legacy scale-2 argument but centres with height 8 -- an off-by-one-scale mismatch the shipped pixels bake in. It is a BRANCH on fs, not a number.",
    "text_field": "fixed 1x metrics: both block prompts draw on the game canvas, so the pads, the caret box and the 8px caret advance never scale. The numbers are data (TF_*), the absence of `* fs` is the quirk.",
    "mini_btn": "unscaled label pads (2, 2): the Settings steppers' vocabulary predates font scaling and its pads never grew. Data (MB_*), unscaled by branch.",
    "chip": "unscaled label clip/min pads (4, 2, 1): a chip's label geometry is in raw pixels while its glyph box is not. Data (CHIP_*), unscaled."
  },
